   "notes": "Waterstones, 22 Sidney St: 1930s-style grey/brown brick front over a stone ground storey with dark Waterstones fascia. First floor has three tall multi-pane windows with wrought-iron balconettes and carved stone oval oculi with garlands above them; plainer windows on the upper floors (top floor not visible). North bay has a separate red panelled door (22a, Vinyl) under a small Waterstones sign. Bay x positions estimated; upper floors over the door bay not clear."
